<title>MONACO: RALLYING-LEADING MONTE CARLO PLACINGS.</title>
<headline>RALLYING-LEADING MONTE CARLO PLACINGS.</headline>
<dateline>MONTE CARLO 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading overall placings in</p>
<p>the Monte Carlo world championship rally after nine timed stages</p>
<p>on Tuesday:</p>
<p>1. Tommi Makinen (Finland) Mitsubishi Lancer  2 hours 28</p>
<p>minutes 19 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Carlos Sainz (Spain) Ford Escort	     2:28:23</p>
<p> 3. Piero Liatti (Italy) Subaru Impreza	  2:28:34</p>
<p> 4. Armin Schwarz (Germany) Ford Escort	  2:31:12</p>
<p> 5. Didier Auriol (France) Ford Escort	   2:32:27</p>
<p> 6. Dieter Depping (Germany) Ford Escort	 2:35:12</p>
<p> 7. Uwe Nittel (Germany) Mitsubishi Lancer     2:35:28</p>
<p> 8. Olivier Burri (Switzerland) Subaru Impreza 2:39:37</p>
<p> 9. Henrik Lundgaard (Denmark) Toyota Celica   2:40:13</p>
<p>10. Gustavo Trelles (Spain) Mitsubishi Lancer 2:41:32</p>
</text>
